    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0436" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/840: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-05-25">May 25, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1345. Department has received from Spanish Embassy memorandum<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d350-f1"/> stating that Japanese Government will transport Americans
                    from Shanghai to Nagasaki and Kobe via S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Conte
                        Verde</hi> leaving Shanghai June 1. Description of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Conte Verde</hi> given in this memorandum is not adequate.</p>
                <p>Please request Swiss Government urgently to inform Japanese Government that
                    American Government must know flag displayed by <hi rendition="#italic">Conte
                        Verde</hi> and distinctive markings on port, starboard, and upper deck of
                    this Vessel.</p>
                <p>Also inform Japanese Government sailing of <hi rendition="#italic">Conte
                        Verde</hi> should be postponed from June 1 to June 7 to permit receipt of
                    desired information by American armed forces.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
